/// <summary>
/// When true, an answer that lands with every talk surface SHUT is spoken anyway — so a
/// question can be asked and then listened to while riding, trading, or reading the map
/// (Anton's ask, 2026.08.16). With it off, a reply only speaks into the thread you are
/// looking at, which is what it did before.
/// <para>
/// It rides UNDER <see cref="VoiceAutoSpeak"/>, never beside it: "speak without being asked"
/// is the promise this is a shape of, and one switch that silences everything must keep
/// meaning that. It is its OWN switch for the same reason reach-outs are — there is one
/// voice at a time, so two answers landing together cut each other off, and a player who
/// wants a voice only while reading should be able to say so without losing the rest.
/// </para>
/// <para>
/// A hosted voice is billed by the minute whether or not anybody is watching, so this is
/// also the one voice setting that can quietly cost money on a reply nobody heard.
/// </para>
/// </summary>
public bool VoiceSpeakWhenClosed { get; set; } = true;

/// <summary>
/// Speaks an answer that has just landed — if it should be heard at all. The ONE place that
/// judgement is made, so the two window shapes and the greeting road cannot drift apart.
/// <para>
/// THREE STATES, not two (2026.08.16, Anton's ask). Looking at this very thread: speak, as it
/// always has. Looking at SOMEBODY ELSE's thread: do not — a voice from a page the player is
/// not on reads as the wrong person talking, and the play mark is one click away. Nothing of
/// ours on stage at all: speak. That last one IS the ask — a question asked and then listened
/// to while riding.
/// </para>
/// <para>
/// It waits out a battle and a live conversation and nothing else (the letters' own rail, which
/// asks the identical question). NOT the reach-out rail: that one also wants the map itself,
/// and being in the inventory is exactly the "doing something else" this is for. A moment that
/// is refused is not deferred — the moment would be gone — the words simply keep their play
/// mark in the thread.
/// </para>
/// </summary>
private void SpeakArrivedWords(Hero npc, string words, bool viewing)
{
    try
    {
        if (npc == null || string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(words)) return;
        if (!Voice.VoiceService.AutoSpeakEnabled) return;

        if (!viewing)
        {
            if (_config?.VoiceSpeakWhenClosed != true) return;
            if (UI.TalkUI.IsOpen) return;        // up, but on another soul's page
            if (!IsSafeForLetterUi()) return;    // a scene or a live talk is in front of them
        }

        Voice.VoiceService.Speak(npc, words);
    }
    catch (Exception ex) { ModLog.Error("voice: speaking an answer that arrived", ex); }
}

