Two refinements to the claim, both affecting the fix.

SEVERITY: for a child of the marriage the *state* change is inert, not damaging - `IsOwnedBeforeTheWorld` (Owned != Withheld) and `AwaitsTheName` read the same either way, and `HouseOfThePlayerLine` filters `!c.InMarriage` (BirthText.cs:171-172), so the house line never changes. The harm is entirely the permanent beats (mother + each child) and the player notice. A fix should therefore not touch the enum semantics; it only needs to stop calling `OwnTheChild` where no question arose.

THE PROPOSED FIX NEEDS A FALLBACK. `if (pick is BirthScale scale) { HoldTheFeast(record, scale); if (mustOwnIt && record.Scale != BirthScale.Unfeasted) OwnTheChild(record, late: false, withFeast: true); }` is right in shape - HoldTheFeast first so a purse emptied since the choosing cannot record a hall that was never kept (it sets `record.Scale` only on success at 967), `mustOwnIt` so a child of the marriage keeps the plain feast it always had, `withFeast: true` so the mother's permanent beat says what actually happened. But it loses the owning entirely when HoldTheFeast bails: `MarkFeastOffered` has already run at 603, so the father is never asked again, and the record strands at `NeverArose` - not `Withheld`, so `AwaitsTheName` is false and `GiveTheNameTo` refuses him the late naming too. He chose to own the child; only the feast failed. So the else must still own it quietly:

    if (pick is BirthScale scale)
    {
        HoldTheFeast(record, scale);
        if (mustOwnIt) OwnTheChild(record, late: false, withFeast: record.Scale != BirthScale.Unfeasted);
    }
    else if (pick as string == QuietOwning) { OwnTheChild(record, late: false); TrySealIfWhole(record); }

Line 607 stays exactly as it is - it is the withFeast:false case and is already correct. Optionally belt-and-braces: give `OwnTheChild` the same `record.BornInMarriage` early return its sibling `WithholdTheName` carries at 685, so no future caller can re-open this. Nothing in BirthText changes; the hall branch simply becomes reachable.
